@startuml
title Secure notes demonstration system context and trust boundaries

left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

actor "Anonymous internet user" as Anonymous
actor "Authenticated user" as User
actor "Administrator" as Admin
actor "Application operator" as Operator
actor "Developer / build input" as Developer

rectangle "Browser to application trust boundary" {
  component "FastAPI server-rendered application\nAuthentication, sessions, CSRF, RBAC, CRUD" as App
}

rectangle "Application to database trust boundary" {
  database "SQLite demonstration database\nAccounts, hashed sessions, encrypted notes, audit records" as DB
}

rectangle "Application to key-source trust boundary" {
  collections "Environment configuration\n32-byte AES-GCM master key" as Keys
}

rectangle "Optional adapter boundary\nNot implemented by this demonstration" {
  component "External notification / monitoring adapter" as External
}

Anonymous --> App : Registration/login fields, headers, cookies, paths,
query parameters, repeated and oversized requests
User --> App : Note content and identifiers, CSRF headers/forms,
export and CRUD requests
Admin --> App : Administrative requests
Operator --> App : Runtime configuration and deployment
Developer --> App : Source, dependencies, build and test inputs

App --> DB : Parameterized SQLAlchemy operations
App --> Keys : Key load; no key stored in database
App ..> External : Future interface only

note bottom of App
Authentication/session boundary separates anonymous and authenticated requests.
Server-side RBAC separates normal-user and administrative operations.
NOTES_ENV defaults to development; production must be selected for non-loopback use.
Development/test settings must not silently become deployed-runtime settings.
end note

note bottom of External
No Kafka, SIEM, MISP/TAXII, OAuth provider,
production email, or production KMS adapter is claimed.
end note
@enduml
